A||||4||FieroDancer||Punctured acceleration.....||||1||
Z||000000||FieroDancer||06-22-2001||01:54 PM||||My 87 5 spd 4 cyl Fiero refuses to drive smoothly. Starts and idles just fine, then drives like it has hick-ups. Service Engine signal comes on - I pump the gas and accelerate fairly hard, then on the decelleration the service engine light goes off again and the motor runs somewhat smooth for 10-15 minutes until this happens again. <BR>I have changed the TPS and the airfilter. Any suggestions? Could it be the O2 sensor?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Posthumane||06-22-2001||04:53 PM||||The first thing you should do is check the computer codes. If the check engine light is coming on, then the computer is sending a fault code. To check for codes, take off the diagnostics terminal cover on your center console and run a jumper wire from the diagnostics pit to the ground pin (the two closest to the passenger side on the lower part of the connector). Then turn your key to on (engine off) and the check engine light will flash out the codes starting with code 12. it will flash each code three times.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Flyguy||06-22-2001||05:22 PM||||also check the heat core mine also did this and it was a heat core leak antifreeze inside the car||||reg||1
Z||000003||TRiAD||06-22-2001||10:03 PM||||How old are the plugs, wires, fuel filter and isn't there an injector on the '87?<P>Check these as well. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||06-23-2001||02:06 AM||||Hey Dancer!<BR>Check the codes, but my WAG is the MAP sensor, just replaced one on a friends Fiero...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
